    Follow-up Report Wizard Views — account_payment_followup Module (PF-003)
    ========================================================================

    Form view and window action for
    `account.followup.report.wizard` — a TransientModel that collects
    filter parameters and produces the Aged Receivables Follow-up
    report in PDF or XLSX format.

    Implements:
      - PF-003: Follow-up report generation with filters, grouping
                options, PDF export, and XLSX export

    The underlying `ir.actions.report` record
    (`action_report_followup_aged_receivables`) is defined in
    `report/followup_report.xml`; this file defines only the wizard
    dialog action (`action_followup_report_wizard`) that opens the
    wizard form.

    Wizard Field Inventory (mirrors wizard/followup_report_wizard.py):
      * Scope:        company_id, currency_id (invisible), target_moves
      * Date range:   date_from, date_to, report_date
      * Customer:     partner_ids (M2M), followup_level_ids (M2M)
      * Aging:        aging_bucket_filter, minimum_amount, include_disputed
      * Grouping:     group_by_salesperson, group_by_country,
                      group_by (computed, readonly),
                      group_by_label (computed, invisible)
      * Options:      include_effectiveness,
                      followup_level_names (computed, readonly),
                      partner_count (computed, readonly)

    Wizard Action Methods (defined on the TransientModel):
      * action_generate_report() — returns ir.actions.report for PDF
      * action_export_xlsx()    — returns ir.actions.act_url for XLSX
      * action_preview()        — alias for action_generate_report

    Odoo 19.0 XML Conventions Applied:
      - ``invisible`` attribute (not ``attrs``) per Odoo 17+ convention
      - Consistent 4-space indentation
      - ``<footer>`` placed inside ``<form>`` but OUTSIDE ``<sheet>``
        so action buttons auto-position at the bottom of the modal
      - Window action uses ``target="new"`` so the form renders as a
        modal dialog rather than a full-page view
-->
<odoo>
    <data>

        <!-- ================================================================
             SECTION 1: FOLLOW-UP REPORT WIZARD FORM VIEW
             Model: account.followup.report.wizard (TransientModel)
             =================================================================
             Collects filter, grouping, and output options from the user
             and surfaces action buttons that dispatch PDF / XLSX / preview
             generation methods on the underlying TransientModel.

             Implements:
               - PF-003 Scenario 1: Generate Aged Receivables Follow-up Report
               - PF-003 Scenario 2: Filter Report by Follow-up Level
               - PF-003 Scenario 4: Export Report to PDF Format
               - PF-003 Scenario 5: Export Report to Excel Format
               - PF-003 Scenario 7: Filter by Date Range and Amount Threshold
               - PF-003 Scenario 8: Group Report by Salesperson or Region
             ================================================================ -->
        <record id="view_account_followup_report_wizard_form" model="ir.ui.view">
            <field name="name">account.followup.report.wizard.form</field>
            <field name="model">account.followup.report.wizard</field>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <form string="Follow-up Report">
                    <sheet>
                        <!-- Title block: describes the report's purpose
                             so users understand what the wizard produces
                             before they configure filters. -->
                        <div class="oe_title">
                            <h1>Aged Receivables Follow-up Report</h1>
                            <p class="text-muted">
                                Configure the filters below to generate a report of
                                outstanding customer balances grouped by aging bucket.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Section 1: Report Scope and Date Range
                             Company selection is gated by the multi-company
                             group so it appears only when the user can
                             actually switch companies.  ``no_create`` prevents
                             accidental creation of a res.company record from
                             the wizard.  currency_id is hidden but MUST be
                             present on the form for the monetary widget on
                             minimum_amount to resolve its currency reference. -->
                        <group string="Report Scope" name="scope_group">
                            <group>
                                <field name="company_id"
                                       options="{'no_create': True}"
                                       groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
                                <field name="currency_id" invisible="1"/>
                                <field name="target_moves"/>
                            </group>
                            <group>
                                <field name="date_from"/>
                                <field name="date_to"/>
                                <field name="report_date"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>

                        <!-- Section 2: Customer Filters
                             Partner and follow-up-level selectors use
                             many2many_tags for compact multi-select display.
                             Empty selection means "include ALL" — the
                             placeholder text communicates this semantics
                             clearly since it differs from the usual
                             "empty = nothing" interpretation of M2M.
                             ``no_create`` prevents creation of partners or
                             follow-up levels from the wizard context. -->
                        <group string="Customer Filters" name="customer_filters_group">
                            <field name="partner_ids"
                                   widget="many2many_tags"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"
                                   placeholder="Leave empty for all customers..."/>
                            <field name="followup_level_ids"
                                   widget="many2many_tags"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"
                                   placeholder="Leave empty for all levels..."/>
                        </group>

                        <!-- Section 3: Aging and Amount Filters (left)
                                        Grouping options (right)
                             The aging bucket filter narrows output to a
                             specific age cohort (Current / 1-30 / 31-60 /
                             61-90 / 90+ / overdue / all).  minimum_amount
                             uses the monetary widget driven by the hidden
                             currency_id declared in Section 1.

                             The grouping side shows booleans for the two
                             user-toggleable group dimensions (salesperson,
                             country) and a readonly ``group_by`` selection
                             that reflects the computed outcome of those
                             booleans, giving the user visual confirmation
                             of the grouping that will be applied.  The
                             ``group_by_label`` field is an internal helper
                             used by the report template and is intentionally
                             hidden from the wizard UI. -->
                        <group>
                            <group string="Aging Filter" name="aging_filter_group">
                                <field name="aging_bucket_filter"/>
                                <field name="minimum_amount"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"/>
                                <field name="include_disputed"/>
                            </group>
                            <group string="Grouping" name="grouping_group">
                                <field name="group_by_salesperson"/>
                                <field name="group_by_country"/>
                                <field name="group_by" readonly="1"/>
                                <field name="group_by_label" invisible="1"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>

                        <!-- Section 4: Report Options
                             ``include_effectiveness`` toggles the collection-
                             effectiveness KPI block (Scenario 6).  The
                             right column shows computed summary feedback:
                               * followup_level_names — human-readable list
                                 of currently-selected levels; hidden when
                                 empty to reduce clutter when no filter
                                 is applied.
                               * partner_count — number of partners matching
                                 the current filters; helps the user gauge
                                 report size before producing a potentially
                                 expensive PDF. -->
                        <group string="Report Options" name="report_options_group">
                            <group>
                                <field name="include_effectiveness"/>
                            </group>
                            <group>
                                <field name="followup_level_names"
                                       readonly="1"
                                       invisible="not followup_level_names"/>
                                <field name="partner_count" readonly="1"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>
                    </sheet>

                    <!-- Footer: action buttons for the wizard.
                         Per Odoo wizard convention, action buttons live in
                         <footer> (NOT inside <sheet>) so they auto-position
                         at the bottom of the modal dialog regardless of
                         sheet scroll state.

                         Button semantics:
                           * Generate PDF (btn-primary)    —
                               Calls action_generate_report() on the
                               wizard; returns the ir.actions.report
                               action that renders the QWeb PDF template
                               defined in report/followup_report.xml.
                           * Export to Excel (btn-secondary) —
                               Calls action_export_xlsx() on the wizard;
                               returns an ir.actions.act_url that
                               streams the XLSX download to the browser.
                           * Preview (btn-secondary)       —
                               Calls action_preview() on the wizard;
                               alias of action_generate_report() that
                               opens the PDF in a preview window rather
                               than as a download.
                           * Cancel (btn-secondary, special)  —
                               Uses Odoo's ``special="cancel"`` so the
                               dialog closes without invoking any action
                               method.  This is the standard pattern for
                               wizard cancel buttons. -->
                    <footer>
                        <button name="action_generate_report"
                                type="object"
                                string="Generate PDF"
                                class="btn-primary"/>
                        <button name="action_export_xlsx"
                                type="object"
                                string="Export to Excel"
                                class="btn-secondary"/>
                        <button name="action_preview"
                                type="object"
                                string="Preview"
                                class="btn-secondary"/>
                        <button string="Cancel"
                                class="btn-secondary"
                                special="cancel"/>
                    </footer>
                </form>
            </field>
        </record>


        <!-- ================================================================
             SECTION 2: WIZARD WINDOW ACTION
             =================================================================
             Entry point referenced from views/menuitem.xml as
             ``action_followup_report_wizard``.  Opens the wizard form
             as a modal dialog (``target="new"``) so the wizard behaves
             as a transient parameter-collection step rather than a
             full-page view.

             Note — this is DISTINCT from the report action
             ``action_report_followup_aged_receivables`` defined in
             report/followup_report.xml.  The chain of invocation is:

               1. User clicks "Follow-ups > Follow-up Report" menu.
               2. This ``action_followup_report_wizard`` opens the
                  wizard form as a modal (target="new").
               3. User configures filters and clicks "Generate PDF".
               4. The wizard's ``action_generate_report()`` returns
                  ``env.ref('account_payment_followup.
                   action_report_followup_aged_receivables')
                   .report_action(self)``.
               5. Odoo renders the QWeb PDF via the report action and
                  streams it to the browser.

             view_mode="form" is mandatory for wizards — TransientModel
             records are not browsable in list/form pairs and must be
             reached through a dedicated dialog. -->
        <record id="action_followup_report_wizard" model="ir.actions.act_window">
            <field name="name">Follow-up Report</field>
            <field name="res_model">account.followup.report.wizard</field>
            <field name="view_mode">form</field>
            <field name="view_id" ref="view_account_followup_report_wizard_form"/>
            <field name="target">new</field>
            <field name="context">{}</field>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
